Remaining battery energy:

\[
1.8\ \text{kWh} - 0.6\ \text{kWh} = 1.2\ \text{kWh}
\]

Heater runtime:

\[
\frac{1.2\ \text{kWh}}{400\ \text{W}}
= \frac{1.2\ \text{kWh}}{0.4\ \text{kW}}
= 3\ \text{h}
\]

**The heater can run for 3 hours.**

Check:

\[
0.6\ \text{kWh} + (0.4\ \text{kW} \times 3\ \text{h})
= 0.6\ \text{kWh} + 1.2\ \text{kWh}
= 1.8\ \text{kWh}
\]

This matches the battery’s usable energy, ignoring other losses.

```js
function groupRuns(values) {
  if (!Array.isArray(values)) {
    throw new TypeError("values must be an array");
  }

  const runs = [];
  const hasOwn = Object.prototype.hasOwnProperty;

  for (let i = 0; i < values.length; i++) {
    if (!hasOwn.call(values, i) || !Number.isInteger(values[i])) {
      throw new TypeError(`values[${i}] must be an integer`);
    }

    const value = values[i];
    const last = runs[runs.length - 1];

    if (last !== undefined && last.value === value) {
      last.count += 1;
    } else {
      runs.push({ value, count: 1 });
    }
  }

  return runs;
}
```

